{
  "analysis": "All three classes fail mostly on small instances: inclusion low-size-tertile recall is 0.075 (146/179 in that tertile, missed median 34.7px vs train median 90.5px), patches 0.467 (51 vs 85px), scratches 0.403 (42 vs 73px). Inclusion is also the starved class (10 real images, AP50 0.179). Round 1 runs a 2x2 factorial vs the balanced/default control: (A) small paste scale only, (B) inclusion-heavy allocation only, (C) both. Scale ranges are set so the expected paste size matches the missed-defect medians (inclusion ~0.3-0.7x, patches/scratches ~0.4-0.8x). Background pool, overlap and source weighting are held at defaults to isolate the two factors.",
  "candidates": [
    {
      "hypothesis": "Small-paste-scale hypothesis: misses concentrate in the low size tertile, so shrinking pastes to the missed size range (inclusion 0.3-0.7x, patches/scratches 0.4-0.8x) should raise small-instance recall. Confirmed if mAP50 beats the balanced/default control, especially inclusion AP50 and low-tertile recall, without a precision collapse.",
      "allocation": {"inclusion": 17, "patches": 17, "scratches": 16},
      "params": {
        "inclusion": {"scale_min": 0.30, "scale_max": 0.70, "target_pool": "same_class", "source_weighting": "uniform", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": []},
        "patches": {"scale_min": 0.40, "scale_max": 0.80, "target_pool": "same_class", "source_weighting": "uniform", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": []},
        "scratches": {"scale_min": 0.40, "scale_max": 0.80, "target_pool": "same_class", "source_weighting": "uniform", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": []}
      }
    },
    {
      "hypothesis": "Allocation hypothesis: inclusion is the starved, worst class (10 real images, AP50 0.179, 148 missed), so at the default scale range, shifting 30 of 50 images to inclusion should lift inclusion AP50 most. Confirmed if inclusion AP50 rises substantially and overall mAP50 beats the balanced control; if not, allocation balance matters less than scale.",
      "allocation": {"inclusion": 30, "patches": 10, "scratches": 10},
      "params": {
        "inclusion": {"scale_min": 0.60, "scale_max": 1.40, "target_pool": "same_class", "source_weighting": "uniform", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": []},
        "patches": {"scale_min": 0.60, "scale_max": 1.40, "target_pool": "same_class", "source_weighting": "uniform", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": []},
        "scratches": {"scale_min": 0.60, "scale_max": 1.40, "target_pool": "same_class", "source_weighting": "uniform", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": []}
      }
    },
    {
      "hypothesis": "Combination hypothesis: if small scale and inclusion-heavy allocation both help, their combination should be the round's best (additive effects). Confirmed if it has the highest mAP50; if it underperforms A or B, the two factors interact negatively and I should not stack them in later rounds.",
      "allocation": {"inclusion": 25, "patches": 12, "scratches": 13},
      "params": {
        "inclusion": {"scale_min": 0.30, "scale_max": 0.70, "target_pool": "same_class", "source_weighting": "uniform", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": []},
        "patches": {"scale_min": 0.40, "scale_max": 0.80, "target_pool": "same_class", "source_weighting": "uniform", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": []},
        "scratches": {"scale_min": 0.40, "scale_max": 0.80, "target_pool": "same_class", "source_weighting": "uniform", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": []}
      }
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Small-scale hypothesis REFUTED: C1 (small, balanced)=0.5417 < control C4 (default, balanced)=0.5667, and C3 (small, incl-heavy)=0.5456 < C2 (default, incl-heavy)=0.5746. Small scale cost ~0.025-0.03 mAP50 in both comparisons, driven by a scratches AP50 collapse (-0.126 in C1); it did lift inclusion/patches modestly, so the harm is class-specific (thin scratches become undetectable when shrunk). Allocation hypothesis CONFIRMED (modestly): inclusion-heavy 30/10/10 at default scale (C2)=0.5746 beat balanced (C4)=0.5667 by +0.008, raising inclusion AP50 0.293->0.3293 and patches too, at a small scratches cost. Combination C3 was not additive because it inherited the small-scale scratches penalty. C2 is the clear best (0.5746, >0.005 above runner-up) and also has the highest worst-class AP50 (0.3293).",
  "choice": 2,
  "lesson": "Shrinking pastes (0.3-0.8x) is a net loss: it helped inclusion/patches but collapsed scratches AP50 (-0.126), so do NOT shrink scratches. Inclusion-heavy allocation (30/10/10) at the default 0.6-1.4 scale was the round's best (0.5746, inclusion 0.329). Next: keep default scale for scratches, try small scale ONLY for inclusion/patches, and probe whether the small scratches cost from inclusion-heavy allocation can be recovered (e.g. slightly more scratches or any_class backgrounds)."
}
